{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:riemannian-covering-metric","title":"prop:riemannian-covering-metric","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":927,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#prop:riemannian-covering-metric","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:smooth-covering-map]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:normal-covering-fibre-transitive]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:covering-automorphism-invariant-metric]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-covering]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/appendixA#prop:elementary-covering-maps]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/appendixC#prop:normal-covering-transitive-action]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#thm:group-action-riemannian-submersion]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:equidimensional-riemannian-submersion-local-isometry]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"prop:riemannian-covering-metric","line":1413,"source":"\\begin{proposition}\n\\label{prop:riemannian-covering-metric}\n\n\\uses{def:smooth-covering-map, def:normal-covering-fibre-transitive, def:covering-automorphism-invariant-metric, def:riemannian-covering, prop:elementary-covering-maps, prop:normal-covering-transitive-action, thm:group-action-riemannian-submersion, prop:equidimensional-riemannian-submersion-local-isometry}\n\n\\dcref{ch2:2.31}\n\n\n\nIf $\\pi:\\tilde M\\to M$ is a smooth normal covering and $\\tilde g$ is invariant under all covering automorphisms, there is a unique metric $g$ on $M$ for which $\\pi$ is a Riemannian covering.\n\\end{proposition}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\sketch Proposition A.49 makes $\\pi$ a surjective smooth submersion; normality gives fiber transitivity of the vertical automorphism action. Theorem \\ref{thm:group-action-riemannian-submersion} gives a unique submersion metric, and injectivity of $d\\pi$ together with Proposition \\ref{prop:equidimensional-riemannian-submersion-local-isometry} identifies it with the unique covering metric.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proposition</div></section> <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-70726f703a7269656d616e6e69616e2d636f766572696e672d6d6574726963\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Asmooth-covering-map\">↗ def:smooth-covering-map</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Anormal-covering-fibre-transitive\">↗ def:normal-covering-fibre-transitive</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Acovering-automorphism-invariant-metric\">↗ def:covering-automorphism-invariant-metric</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ariemannian-covering\">↗ def:riemannian-covering</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FappendixA%23prop%3Aelementary-covering-maps\">↗ prop:elementary-covering-maps</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FappendixC%23prop%3Anormal-covering-transitive-action\">↗ prop:normal-covering-transitive-action</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23thm%3Agroup-action-riemannian-submersion\">↗ thm:group-action-riemannian-submersion</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Aequidimensional-riemannian-submersion-local-isometry\">↗ prop:equidimensional-riemannian-submersion-local-isometry</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch2:2.31</span></span><p></p>If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\pi :\\tilde M\\to M$\">$\\pi :\\tilde M\\to M$</span> is a smooth normal covering and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\tilde g$\">$\\tilde g$</span> is invariant under all covering automorphisms, there is a unique metric <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$g$\">$g$</span> on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span> for which <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\pi $\">$\\pi $</span> is a Riemannian covering.  <p></p><section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p>\\sketch Proposition A.49 makes <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\pi $\">$\\pi $</span> a surjective smooth submersion; normality gives fiber transitivity of the vertical automorphism action. Theorem <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23thm%3Agroup-action-riemannian-submersion\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#thm:group-action-riemannian-submersion\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-74686d3a67726f75702d616374696f6e2d7269656d616e6e69616e2d7375626d657273696f6e\">3</a> gives a unique submersion metric, and injectivity of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$d\\pi $\">$d\\pi $</span> together with Proposition <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Aequidimensional-riemannian-submersion-local-isometry\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:equidimensional-riemannian-submersion-local-isometry\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-70726f703a6571756964696d656e73696f6e616c2d7269656d616e6e69616e2d7375626d657273696f6e2d6c6f63616c2d69736f6d65747279\">8</a> identifies it with the unique covering metric. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:equidimensional-riemannian-submersion-local-isometry","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:riemannian-quotient-metric","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:smooth-covering-map","title":"def:smooth-covering-map","label":"def:smooth-covering-map"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:normal-covering-fibre-transitive","title":"def:normal-covering-fibre-transitive","label":"def:normal-covering-fibre-transitive"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:covering-automorphism-invariant-metric","title":"def:covering-automorphism-invariant-metric","label":"def:covering-automorphism-invariant-metric"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-covering","title":"def:riemannian-covering","label":"def:riemannian-covering"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/appendixA#prop:elementary-covering-maps","title":"prop:elementary-covering-maps","label":"prop:elementary-covering-maps"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/appendixC#prop:normal-covering-transitive-action","title":"prop:normal-covering-transitive-action","label":"prop:normal-covering-transitive-action"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#thm:group-action-riemannian-submersion","title":"thm:group-action-riemannian-submersion","label":"thm:group-action-riemannian-submersion"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:equidimensional-riemannian-submersion-local-isometry","title":"prop:equidimensional-riemannian-submersion-local-isometry","label":"prop:equidimensional-riemannian-submersion-local-isometry"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:riemannian-quotient-metric","title":"prop:riemannian-quotient-metric","label":"prop:riemannian-quotient-metric"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:riemannian-covering-metric","title":"prop:riemannian-covering-metric","tex":"\\begin{proposition}\n\\label{prop:riemannian-covering-metric}\n\n\\uses{def:smooth-covering-map, def:normal-covering-fibre-transitive, def:covering-automorphism-invariant-metric, def:riemannian-covering, prop:elementary-covering-maps, prop:normal-covering-transitive-action, thm:group-action-riemannian-submersion, prop:equidimensional-riemannian-submersion-local-isometry}\n\n\\dcref{ch2:2.31}\n\n\n\nIf $\\pi:\\tilde M\\to M$ is a smooth normal covering and $\\tilde g$ is invariant under all covering automorphisms, there is a unique metric $g$ on $M$ for which $\\pi$ is a Riemannian covering.\n\\end{proposition}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\sketch Proposition A.49 makes $\\pi$ a surjective smooth submersion; normality gives fiber transitivity of the vertical automorphism action. Theorem \\ref{thm:group-action-riemannian-submersion} gives a unique submersion metric, and injectivity of $d\\pi$ together with Proposition \\ref{prop:equidimensional-riemannian-submersion-local-isometry} identifies it with the unique covering metric.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"referen